 the wife who was waiting  for her husband to finish his undercover  assignment before getting a divorce this  leads to dokes being on the radar of the  cartel boss who ordered their murders  and the victim's brother who's also a  cop is giving him trouble about the  affair it all wraps up with james  getting kidnapped by the drug lord and  then that turns out to be a trap set by  the brother who swoops in to make an  arrest also dokes gets involved with a  haitian man who he sees walking across  the bridge he jumps out of the car and  kills him before angel catches up doke  says the victim shot first but angel  doesn't believe that's how it went down  based on what he heard he eventually  decides to tell the truth after being  pushed by internal affairs only to find  out that they dropped the case in the  end this establishes that angel is more  or less an honest cop and that dokes has  a secret past that laguerta and angel  think might be related to the cia or  black ops because of how it played out  beyond that angel is separated from his  wife he had an affair and he told her  about it because of that honesty and  eventually gets a divorce deb struggles  to make her way in the homicide unit and  legueta clearly doesn't like her and  tries to hold her back maria has her own  problems with captain matthews who views  her as a threat and after some political  maneuvering that goes back and forth he  ends up replacing her in his personal  relationships dex works through his  intimacy issues with rita and once their  relationship starts to be somewhat  normal her ex-husband gets released  early from prison paul who was  physically abusive and refused to sign  divorce papers tries to reconcile with  rita who isn't interested he lays it on  heavy with the kids despite him being an  awful person he does seem to love them  rita grants him supervised weekly visits  in exchange for the divorce but he  eventually shows up her house drunk one  night and tries to force himself on her  she hits him with a bat in self-defense  and he manages to turn that around  filing charges for assault in an effort  to win custody this all proves to be  annoying for dexter he ends up getting  involved knocking paul out with a frying  pan in rita's kitchen after they have  some words and then he takes him back to  his room and sets him up by injecting  him with heroin so that he'll violate  his parole in prison paul has no idea  how he got there he suspects that  dexter's involved but he can't remember  how things happened and he realizes that  he was missing a shoe when he got  arrested he pesters rita by phone he's  trying to implicate dexter and she  pretty much ignores him because their  relationship is going really well by the  end of the season though she finds the  shoe and is forced to think that dex  might have been involved in what  happened  while all of this is going on the ice  truck killer case is looming over the  miami metro police department he's a  serial killer that dismembers the bodies  of his victims after draining their  blood this leaves an impression on all  the responders at the crime scene at a  motel in the pilot episode including  dexter the ammo matches two previous  victims that were discovered in nearby  broward county and the discovery of  another in the first episode makes it  pretty clear that the crimes are related  and that they're the work of a serial  killer while talking with deb who  mentions that the body parts were cold  at the last crime scene dexter guesses  he might be using a refrigerated truck  and when this turns out to be the case  he earns the name the ice truck killer  things get personal with the case when  dexter sees a refrigerated truck follows  it only to get the head of one of the  victims tossed at his car later when he  returns to his apartment he finds the  head of a doll stuck on his refrigerator  inside he discovers the rest of the doll  cut up in the same way that the victims  were at the crime scenes as the  investigation continues it has effects  on the department like deb finding the  truck and that getting her promoted to  homicide a couple of wrong suspects are  named as the killer and that sets off  the tensions between the captain and  legueta and this situation establishes  the precedent of dexter wanting to solve  the case for his own selfish reasons  before the police get a chance to make  an arrest the first suspect that the  department focuses on that turns out to  be innocent is a security guard named  tony tucci he was forced to place body  parts of a victim at the ice rink he  worked at while it was all caught on  camera later his body parts started  showing up at different locations in  miami that only dexter knew were tied to  his childhood memories that the ice  truck killer learned about from looking  at photos inside of his apartment dex is  lured to an old closed down hospital  where he finds tony who's missing those  body parts but still alive he's  presented on a kill table with knives at  the ready but dexter decides not to kill  him because he doesn't fit the criteria  of the code instead he tips off deb  anonymously and she's able to rescue him  and get him to a hospital there she  meets his prosthetist rudy cooper who  over time sweeps her off her feet as  their relationship develops it becomes  pretty clear that he's really interested  in getting close to dexter but he does a  good job of keeping that fact from her  and she falls in love with him in the  same episode that she makes the  relationship public with her co-workers  rudy is revealed to be the ice truck  killer when you see him alone in his  apartment that has the walk-in freezer  by this time he's done a lot in the way  of communicating with dexter killer to  killer the head on the truck the dolls  the body parts and locations from his  photos leaving tony for an easy kill  messages on craigslist and he even  resurfaced the body of dex's victim  valerie castillo 