 and it was all built on the  foundation of harry's code as dexter  starts to remember his mother's death  and begins to realize that harry kept  information from him he begins to  question everything you see him struggle  with his reality throughout season one  at one point he decides not to kill  jeremy downes after learning about him  being raped by his victim and they have  a conversation in jail after jeremy  kills again the idea of him doing it  just because he wanted to feel something  and dexter understanding that it calls  into question the idea of killing being  justified as simply taking out the trash  it shows that dexter also does it  because he gets something from it he  gets off on it and jeremy's choosing  suicide is an example of a different  path while he tells himself that what  he's doing is righteous he actively  misleads everyone around him and only  recognizes this as a problem that he  mostly justifies away when he hurts  deborah rita in the process in the  beginning of the season he doesn't think  he has feelings and believes the only  way he can survive is to rely on the  code since he has a secret life he can't  confide in anyone when he has a dilemma  and this is why he manifests harry in  his mind to try to work everything out  himself so by the end what brian offered  him was what he truly wanted someone he  could be himself around and someone that  would accept that he had to kill when he  killed his brother he lost something  real and proved that he does have  feelings by choosing deb and mourning  brian at the end he imagines people  celebrating him for it and even being  thankful for his other kills in that  he's making the world a better place as  a result deep down though he knows that  they would also recognize the brutality  in his form of justice and would likely  think of him as a monster if they knew  the truth by the time everything is  wrapped up he's able to keep his secret  the police have their man and his  adoptive sister is safe things can  mostly return to normal unfortunately on  her way to take out the trash rita  notices paul's shoe right where he said  it would be dexter sees that doakes is  now following him because he knows he  has something to hide and there's no one  left alive that can handle his truth he  learned a lot about himself in the first  season he revealed a lot about his  childhood and how he became what he is  but it served to make him question his  beliefs and that seems like the perfect  place to leave things  please like this video if you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already be sure to check back  for more dexter videos and thanks for  watching i'll talk to you soon

